  "equipment_type": "Indoor pool dehumidifier (air handler) controller",
  "applies_to": "Seresco NE and NV indoor pool units and OA make-up air units (plus the NP and NW series columns in the same table) with the CommandCenter controller.",
  "summary": "Seresco's CommandCenter controller uses one BACnet object list across its NE/NV pool units, OA make-up air units and the NP/NW series; the source marks each object as standard or optional per series. Sensors are AI objects, setpoints and analog outputs are AV objects, and component status, modes, commands and alarms are BV objects. The BMS can override any sensor by setting it Out Of Service and writing its value, with a heartbeat timer to fall back to the unit's sensors. Command objects must first be enabled at the unit.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "BACnet objects document 5.8.0",
  "default_device_instance": 150,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The source has no read/write column; access here follows its text: setpoints (except AV 13), AV 512/515 and the command BVs 512-526 are writable, everything else read-only.",
    "Each description lists the series where the object is standard (Std) or optional (opt); optional objects only appear when that feature is configured.",
    "Temperatures follow the unit's °F/°C keypad setting.",
    "Default device name is 'Seresco Dehumidifier', segmentation is not supported and max APDU is 1476.",
    "The heartbeat text refers to sensor override objects 128-131 that are not in the object tables.",
    "All command BVs (512-526) are marked optional in the source and must be enabled at the unit before they respond."
  ],
