  "integration": {
    "summary": "Enable the BACnet command objects at the unit first. Then use Blower Enabled (BV 512) for start/stop and Occupied (BV 516) for occupancy, and write the room temperature, humidity and pool setpoints (AV 0-2). Monitor the blower contactor, the mode BVs, return air conditions and the alarm count. If the BMS supplies sensor values, set the heartbeat timer (AV 515) so the unit falls back to its own sensors.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 512",
        "name": "Blower Enabled",
        "why": "Start/stop the blower; stopping it stops the unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 516",
        "name": "Occupied",
        "why": "Occupancy command (active = occupied)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "Room Temperature Setpoint",
        "why": "Room air setpoint, 55-95 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Humidity Setpoint",
        "why": "Room RH setpoint, 35-85 %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Pool Temperature Setpoint",
        "why": "Pool water setpoint, 60-108 °F (pool units)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 0",
        "name": "Blower Contactor",
        "why": "Blower running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 260",
        "name": "Dehumidification Mode",
        "why": "Unit is dehumidifying"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "Return Air Humidity",
        "why": "Return (space) air RH, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Return Air Temperature",
        "why": "Return (space) air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 518",
        "name": "Alarm Count",
        "why": "Number of alarms; no single alarm flag exists"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Command objects (BV 512-526) only work after they are enabled at the unit itself. BV 512 Blower Enabled starts and stops the main blower; stopping it stops all other components except a pool unit's auxiliary pool heater. BV 516 Occupied replaces the built-in occupancy scheduler. BV 524/525 A/C and Heat Override take over room temperature control and stay in effect until the unit restarts.",
    "heartbeat": "AV 515 Heartbeat Timer (0-600 s) applies when the BMS supplies sensor values. With a value above 0, the unit returns to its own sensors if no BACnet message arrives within that time, so BMS-written sensor values must be refreshed within the timer even if unchanged. 0 disables the fallback.",
    "remote_sensors": "Any AI sensor can be taken over by setting its Out_Of_Service property to True and writing Present_Value from the BMS. Set AV 515 above 0 so the unit falls back to its installed sensors if BACnet communication stops.",
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance is 150; default device name is 'Seresco Dehumidifier'.",
      "Segmentation is not supported; max APDU length is 1476.",
      "Reinitialize Device supports Warm Start only and needs the password given in the source document."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Command BVs do nothing until enabled at the unit.",
      "A/C and Heat Override (BV 524/525) keep control until a system restart once activated.",
      "Compressor data is only reliable when the matching Available BV (264-266) is active.",
      "AV 13 Humidity Floating Setpoint can't be written; the wall temperature sensor sets it."
    ]
  }
}
